.\" Hand-maintained \(em regenerate nothing, just edit this when the CLI in
.\" src/keycard/cli.py changes. Keep it in sync with `keycard --help`.
.TH KEYCARD 1 "2026-08-07" "keycard 0.1.1" "keycard manual"
.SH NAME
keycard \- disposable SSH sandboxes. One command, zero setup.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keycard
.I command
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B keycard
is a purpose-built SSH server that provisions a disposable container on
connect and destroys it on disconnect. The username in the SSH request
selects the environment:
.PP
.RS
ssh ubuntu@host    ->  a clean Linux box
.br
ssh python@host    ->  Python, nothing else
.br
ssh node@host      ->  Node, nothing else
.RE
.PP
There is no client to install and nothing to configure. A
.I keycard.toml
file is read if present, but every default works with zero setup.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B up
Run the keycard server. Blocks until interrupted (Ctrl-C, SIGINT, or
SIGTERM), at which point it stops accepting new connections, gives
connected sessions a grace period to finish, and then exits.
.TP
.B rooms
List the environments the running configuration would offer, along with
each room's resource caps and network setting, then exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "keycard up"
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Path to
.IR keycard.toml .
Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/keycard/keycard.toml ,
falling back to the built-in rooms if that file doesn't exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " ADDRESS"
Address to bind. Overrides the
.I listen
value from config.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Port to listen on. Overrides the
.I listen
value from config.
.TP
.BI \-\-keep " DURATION"
Pause a room on disconnect instead of destroying it, for
.I DURATION
(e.g.
.IR 10m )
to allow the same username to reconnect and resume it. Overrides the
.I keep_window
value from config; unset or
.I 0
disables the feature.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable debug logging.
.SS "keycard rooms"
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Path to
.IR keycard.toml ,
same as above.
.SS "Global"
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the keycard version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage for
.B keycard
or any subcommand and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/keycard/keycard.toml
Optional configuration: listen address, timeouts, and custom
.RI [ rooms.* ]
entries. See
.I keycard.example.toml
in the project repository for every available key.
.TP
.I ~/.config/keycard/authorized_keys
Public keys permitted to connect, in OpenSSH
.I authorized_keys
format. Required \(em keycard refuses to start without it.
.TP
.I ~/.config/keycard/host_key
The server's ed25519 host key, generated on first run and kept
thereafter. Regenerating it breaks host-key verification for every
existing client.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The
.B up
process itself exits 0 on a clean shutdown, or non-zero if it could not
start (for example, a missing
.IR authorized_keys ).
.PP
Within a single SSH session connected to a room, the exit status seen by
the client is normally whatever the shell inside the room exited with.
Two values are reserved for keycard's own housekeeping:
.TP
.B 124
The room was destroyed by the idle-timeout reaper (no traffic for
.IR idle_timeout ),
following the same convention as GNU coreutils'
.BR timeout (1).
.TP
.B 143
The session was cut short because the server was shutting down, after
its
.I shutdown_grace
period expired \(em the same code a shell reports for a process killed
by SIGTERM (128 + 15).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the server with defaults:
.B keycard up
.TP
Bind to a specific host and port, with debug logging:
.B keycard up \-\-host 0.0.0.0 \-\-port 2222 \-v
.TP
Allow a 10-minute reconnect window after a dropped connection:
.B keycard up \-\-keep 10m
.TP
See what a given config would offer:
.B keycard rooms \-\-config ./keycard.toml
.TP
Connect from a client, once the server is running:
.B ssh \-p 2222 python@yourhost
.SH SECURITY
Containers are hygiene, not an isolation boundary \(em see
.I SECURITY.md
in the project repository for the full threat model before exposing
keycard beyond a trusted network.
.SH AUTHOR
Sam Truss
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR docker (1)
.PP
Project homepage: https://github.com/SamTruss/keycard
